{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/13329-my-mummy-gamet","id":13329,"title":"My Mummy Gamet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T05:04:29-08:00","id":13329,"title":"My Mummy Gamet","content":"I've been running a game of Mummy for a while now with my girlfriend and two of our friends. We haven't been able to play as often as I have liked due to conflicting schedules but we are close to finishing the second story and closing in on the BIG reveal. I am a big supporter of playing games &quot;my way&quot; so I wanted to share with you how we've been playing the game, and include some of the plot.<br /> <br /> A big theme in the game is memory and forgotten mistakes. The players may have realized the latter part by now but I've been keeping it to myself most of the time. We don't focus much on the Guilds or the Judges and most of the chronicle has focused on Memory. So here's how I put focus on it:<br /> <br /> We did not have a special character creation session. The players didn't know this, but I handed them empty character sheets and said &quot;You arise.&quot; They got to distribute 12 points freely among their Attributes and 22 points among their Skills, and all the rest as normal, but they did not have to do it right away. You could distribute the points while we were playing, essentially remembering what they were capable of. At the end of the first session, they would finish distributing the remaining points (I did this so we wouldn't have to keep track of what they had already finished and what they had left).<br /> <br /> They also got 40 exp to spend, but could spend this at any time. I gave them 40 because they would not earn any experience points during play or at the end of the session. This was past experience, which they would recall during play. I also told them that if they would come up with a cool backstory for why their characters had learned this or that, I would reward them Sebayt experience. This brought up some cool stuff like one Mummy learning how to use a gun in WWI when she was protecting the Cult during wartime. In addition, if anyone would increase their Memory rating they would play out a flashback of forgotten event that would tie in with the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:05:02-08:00","id":13330,"title":"","content":"The first story began in 1938, Austria. Their Cult wanted to move the Tomb due to the Nazis and needed the Mummies' blessing and assistance. When a small group of Nazi soldiers came by, hoping to obtain the Mummies from the Cult before they would arise and shot the High Priest's son, the Mummies responded with godly fury by ripping the SS officer's head off (who turned out to be a vampire), crushing another soldier with the very vehicle they arrived in and basically scaring the others mindless (and then killing them). By searching the SS officer, the Mummies found out that they had been sent by someone named Blutgraben.<br /> <br /> They traveled to a nearby town called Wunderstadt where they found another Mummy named Neith. After being captured and brought to Neith, she bowed to one of the PC Mummies (at which point we ended that session, with the player's jaw dropped) and revealed she belonged to the same Guild and was of lower status. After causing some trouble in her town, she gave them the option of either killing one of the PC Mummies' Cult members as punishment (she was the cause anyway) or that the Mummies would go collect a specific vessel which Neith believed that Blutgraben was transporting not far away. It was revealed that the trouble-making Cultist was the former lover of one of the Mummies 20 years earlier, when they last arose, and was quite mad after the experience. Another jaw dropped.<br /> <br /> Neith also revealed that Blutgraben was a secret society that within the Nazi party, believed to be run by vampires. When one of the PC Mummies increased his Memory, a long forgotten event was revealed to him. He and Neith had gone to collect a Relic from a rival Cult, but he was stabbed in the back (literally) by Neith who took the Relic for herself. The Mummies decided not to act on it and escaped any punishment for the Cultist's crime by offering Neith an ominous looking statue that had some unknown power and was of unknown origin. Between you and me, they could have defeated Neith easily, but they knew they would put their own Cult at risk since Neith's Cult was bigger and better armed. They left Wunderstadt and that is where the story ended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:05:39-08:00","id":13331,"title":"","content":"Next story began in 1986, in America. The former High Priest was dead, and the Cult that had mostly been a large family of three siblings and their descendants had grown under new leadership into a noteworthy organization. The Mummies started this new story with 60 experience points. I told them I would allow them to buy any Merit that was &quot;Character creation only&quot; simply by saying &quot;You're bigger than I remembered&quot; (Giant), but nobody used it. They found out that stuff had happened. Only the decedents of the former High Priest remained, his sister and family were all dead, his brother and the brother's son were either dead or missing (the old HP's brother appeared to be conspiring and manipulated his son a lot, so the Mummies did not miss that guy) and the Cultist who was madly in love and caused the fuss in Wunderstadt had been at an asylum for the past 20-30 years. The former HP's grandson was now the new High Priest and had built the Cult into this influential organization (which was obviously criminal).<br /> <br /> A name would also come up: Alben Brugt, CEO of Sanguine Medical, operated from Germany but extending all over the world. The Mummies found out that Alben Brugt is an anagram for Blutgraben, and figured it would be something they would have to look out for.<br /> <br /> They were sent to save the nHP's daughter from a previous marriage. Another player increased her Mummy's Memory remembering a meeting with a vampire in Rome more than 2000 years ago. On the way back the last Mummy increased her Memory, reliving the moment when she killed the old HP's sister and her family, but perishing in the resulting fire. Suddenly the players didn't like the new HP as much. When they got closer to home, they sensed danger in the Tomb. Once hurried back, the saw it being attacked and realized that their mission had been a diversion to get them away from their Tomb and Cult.<br /> <br /> After stopping the attack and saving the new HP, they found out that the High Priest's current wife had lead the attack but someone else had orchestrated it, namely the old HP's sister's son (who was supposed to be dead). Another jaw drop, and that's where we ended the session and haven't played again yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:30:32-08:00","id":13344,"title":"","content":"&quot;Wunderstadt&quot;<br /> <br /> hee hee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:42:20-08:00","id":13350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/13329-my-mummy-gamet?p=13344#post13344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Wunderstadt&quot;<br /> <br /> hee hee.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also how they reacted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:50:35-08:00","id":28382,"title":"","content":"Finally had another session earlier tonight.<br /> <br /> The Mummies confronted Hans Heller, the man who orchestrated the attack on the tomb. They could have gotten some information out of him but instead they aggravated him enough for him to detonate an explosive. The explosive didn't seem to be specifically effective against the mummies, but Heller was killed. They found a man who was watching the whole thing and reporting back to someone, and managed to find out that Julian Cornelius, a man who was working with Alben Brugt, aka Blutgraben, had hired him and paid all of Heller's expenses.<br /> <br /> Reporting back to HP, the HP ordered them to handle the problem and make sure that Sanguine Medical's office in the city would no longer pose a problem. The Mummies were not entirely pleased with the plan but went to Cornelius's office to confront him. They suspected him to be a vampire, since he only worked during the night when he could be in direct contact with Alben Brugt in Germany, allegedly.<br /> <br /> After killing the only two guards in the building, they figured it was odd how it was hardly secured at all. They found out that Cornelius was indeed in his office, and had sent everyone home. He was waiting for them. When they confronted him, he bowed, and welcomed one of them as the goddess he had been worshiping for the past 2000 years. He explained how there was no real Blutgraben, that it had all been orchestrated by one of them two thousand years earlier. Since that time, he had been building a new Cult, one that spanned the entire world through Sanguine Medical. As planned, Cornelius had been attempting to rid the Mummies of their current Cult, one that they had hated from the very beginning when they saved them from Egypt (or so the story goes), but had lost the Mummies when they left Rome. During the early years of the century, the new Cult attempted a method of elimination by manipulating the Nazis. Finally, Hans Heller offered an opportunity to directly attack the old Cult's headquarters. The explosive was unfortunate, but they had managed to reduce its force without Heller finding out.<br /> <br /> Cornelius offered the Mummies the service of a world-wide Cult, one that had been in the works for a long time. They only needed to leave their old Cult behind. They agreed.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> It was a plot twist I had been planning a long time. A powerful enemy working in the shadows and they find out that it was one of them all along. I was really happy so see their reaction as they found out. The chronicle isn't planned to be any longer than this, but I've told the players that I'm keeping the option open just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:57:07-08:00","id":28423,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of coming up with a reason for how you learned to use something, like the WWI gun. Also, that each dot of Memory brings on a relevant flashback","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:53:55-07:00","id":138515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/13329-my-mummy-gamet#post13329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did not have a special character creation session. The players didn't know this, but I handed them empty character sheets and said &quot;You arise.&quot; They got to distribute 12 points freely among their Attributes and 22 points among their Skills, and all the rest as normal, but they did not have to do it right away. You could distribute the points while we were playing, essentially remembering what they were capable of. At the end of the first session, they would finish distributing the remaining points (I did this so we wouldn't have to keep track of what they had already finished and what they had left).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just ridiculously clever. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:58:55-07:00","id":138527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/13329-my-mummy-gamet?p=138515#post138515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is just ridiculously clever. Well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is... man I'm kind of glad my ST wouldn't do this because I almost always have my characters set in stone the moment I think one up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T01:28:55-07:00","id":139110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/13329-my-mummy-gamet?p=138515#post138515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is just ridiculously clever. Well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The players did have different tactics dealing with this. While two of them used the opportunity to arrange their points as was needed, one of them was too busy assigning points to follow the plot and finished her character before the scene was over. It slowed the game down a bit since we waited for her to finish, but all in all I enjoyed doing this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":""